@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+Concrete satisfying witnesses for the three submitted claims
+=============================================================
+
+Inner-loop claim:
+  REST = .K, C = 5, X = 77, _I = 78, _N = 100.
+  Initial <k>: INNER-LOOP ~> .K
+  Initial <env>:
+    "count" |-> 5
+    "i"     |-> 78
+    "n"     |-> 100
+    "x"     |-> 77
+  Precondition: 77 >= 0 (true).
+  Claimed destination: count = 5 + digitSevens(77) = 7, x = 0,
+  with i and n unchanged and <k> = .K.
+
+Outer-loop claim:
+  REST = Return(Name("count")), C = 0, I = 0, N = 79.
+  Initial <k>: OUTER-LOOP ~> Return(Name("count"))
+  Initial <env>:
+    "count" |-> 0
+    "i"     |-> 0
+    "n"     |-> 79
+    "x"     |-> 0
+  Precondition: 0 >= 0 and 0 <= 79 (true).
+  Claimed destination before REST: count = fizzFrom(0,79) = 3,
+  i = 79, n = 79, x = 0.
+
+End-to-end entry claim:
+  N = 79.
+  Initial state is exactly the claim's Module(FuncDef(...)) term, <input> 79,
+  <env> .Map, and <result> 0. There is no requires-clause, so this state
+  satisfies its precondition.
+  Claimed destination: <k> .K; count/result = fizzFrom(0,79) = 3;
+  i = fizzEnd(79) = 79; n = 79; x = 0.
+
